flowchart TD
    %% Standard DFD Shapes and Data Flow Standards
    classDef process fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#2e7d32,stroke-width:2px,rx:10,ry:10;
    classDef entity fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1565c0,stroke-width:2px,shape:rect;
    classDef store fill:#fff3e0,stroke:#ef6c00,stroke-width:2px,shape:cylinder;

    %% Entities
    Student[Student]:::entity
    Counselor[Counselor]:::entity
    
    %% Processes (Functionality - Circle/Oval for DFD)
    P1((1.0 Validate User)):::process
    P2((2.0 Check Availability)):::process
    P3((3.0 Process Booking)):::process
    P4((4.0 Generate Notification)):::process
    
    %% Data Stores (Open Rectangle or Cylinder)
    D1[(Users DB)]:::store
    D2[(Appointments DB)]:::store
    D3[(Notifications DB)]:::store

    %% Data Flows (NOUNS ONLY - Representing Data Packets)
    Student -->|Login Credentials| P1
    P1 <-->|User Profile Data| D1
    
    P1 -->|Validated User ID| P2
    P2 <-->|Schedule Slot Information| D2
    
    Student -->|Booking Request & Wellness Data| P3
    P3 -->|New Appointment Record| D2
    
    P3 -->|Appointment Detail Packet| P4
    P4 -->|Alert Data Record| D3
    P4 -->|Email Confirmation Content| Counselor